From 2d7ae9dc639b0a0ddc01301e9260998602a92f96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 09:38:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add declining-balance waterfall option, pricing bridge,
 and return/timing analytics

Round-2 gaps against the real secondaries pricing template:
- apply_carry_waterfall_declining_balance(): an alternate European waterfall where
  a hurdle balance rolls forward (grows by the preferred return on itself, shrinks
  as distributions are applied to it) instead of comparing against a single
  compounded threshold. Both are legitimate, kept side by side via a sidebar
  toggle -- the existing compounded-threshold waterfall stays the default.
- cash_flow_duration(): distribution-weighted average time until cash comes back.
- New "Analytics & Pricing Bridge" tab: Gross (GP-reported, optional input) vs Net
  (LP actual) to-date performance, MV CAGR, cash-flow duration, RV/MV multiple
  (portfolio mode), MOIC unadjusted (TVPI) vs adjusted for CFs (seller-scenario
  MOIC), and a Reported Value -> Market Value -> Gross Exposure -> Net Funded
  Exposure -> Net Effective Price bridge.
- Portfolio mode's EV/EBITDA expander now also shows each company's full
  Revenue/EBITDA/FCF/Net Debt year-by-year schedule, not just the summary metrics.

Verified with 20 independent checks in test_v3_features.py (manual re-derivation,
not re-calling the functions under test) plus 10 Streamlit AppTest smoke
combinations covering every new feature alone and combined with round-1's.

